<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Use | StackAutopsy Web3 Security Suite"
  description="Plain-English Terms of Use for StackAutopsy: local browser software, no custody, no accounts, voluntary donations."
  heading="Terms of Use"
>
  <p class="card p-4 text-sm text-ink">
    <strong>In plain English:</strong> StackAutopsy is read-only diagnostic software that runs inside your own
    browser. We never hold your coins or keys, never execute trades, and never charge fees. Any donations are strictly
    voluntary. Always verify important results yourself and never enter seed phrases or private keys.
  </p>
  <h2>§ 1 Scope</h2>
  <p>
    These terms of use govern the use of the software suite "StackAutopsy — Web3 Security &amp; Forensics Suite"
    (hereinafter the "Suite"), provided by <strong>AndrexTheDev</strong>
    (contact: <strong>hippie.highho@gmail.com</strong>). By accessing and using the Suite you agree to
    these terms. Deviating terms of the user do not apply.
  </p>

  <h2>§ 2 Service description and regulatory delimitation</h2>
  <p>
    The Suite is a <strong>purely local diagnostic, formatting and analysis software</strong>. All
    calculations, decodings and signature checks take place in the user's browser. In particular,
    <strong>none</strong> of the following activities take place:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>no custody or administration of crypto assets or cryptographic keys for third parties,</li>
    <li>no order execution, no order routing and no operation of liquidity pools or trading platforms,</li>
    <li>no intermediation of transactions and no exchange service,</li>
    <li>no charging of transaction fees or other remuneration for on-chain operations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The Suite therefore provides no services within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2023/1114 (MiCA) and no
    financial or crypto-asset services requiring authorization under supervisory law. Prepared transaction data
    (calldata, authorization tuples) is made available exclusively to the user for their own responsible review
    and optional execution via their own wallet.
  </p>

  <h2>§ 3 Voluntary support (donations)</h2>
  <p>
    Use of the Suite creates <strong>no contractual obligation to pay</strong> on the part of the user towards the
    operator. Notwithstanding this, users may voluntarily support the operator via the on-chain addresses shown
    in the interface. Voluntary support payments:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>create <strong>no exchange contract</strong> and no claim to consideration, support, SLAs or feature unlocks,</li>
    <li>obligate the operator to nothing and create no warranty claims,</li>
    <li>are technically final blockchain transactions that cannot be charged back or refunded,</li>
    <li>are made solely at the user's decision from the user's own wallet.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>§ 4 Duties of the user</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>to independently and professionally verify results before making decisions based on them,</li>
    <li>not to enter private keys or seed phrases into tool fields (the Suite actively blocks such input where technically detectable),</li>
    <li>to fulfil legal obligations (tax, reporting and record-keeping duties) themselves,</li>
    <li>to regenerate pre-signed emergency packages (e.g.&nbsp;panic revoke) after every nonce change.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>§ 5 Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The Suite is made available to the user without any contractual obligation to pay.
    Against this background, the operator's liability — regardless of the legal basis — is limited to intent and gross
    negligence; liability for simple negligence is excluded to the extent permitted by law.
    This does not apply to damage from injury to life, body or health, nor under
    mandatory statutory provisions (e.g.&nbsp;product liability law).
  </p>
  <p>
    No liability is accepted for the correctness of external blockchain data, the availability of external
    endpoints, or for damage resulting from incorrect operation, wallet software or network conditions.
  </p>

  <h2>§ 6 Intellectual property and permitted use</h2>
  <p>
    The "StackAutopsy" brand, texts, design and source-code organization of the Suite are subject to the operator's
